# PUBLIC AVAILABILITY WITH SOURCE-CODE VISIBILITY LICENSE

## Version 1.0 (PASVL-1.0)

**Short identifier:** `LicenseRef-PASVL-1.0`
**Steward:** Bangladesh Software Development Community (BSDC)
**Document status:** Published, in force from 2026-01-01
**Canonical URL:** https://github.com/bsdc-info-bd/PASVL_LOSDA/blob/main/LICENSE
**Human-readable summary (non-binding):** [legal/plain-language.md](legal/plain-language.md)

---

### PREAMBLE

Software is written to be seen, studied, audited, trusted, and improved. Software is also
written by people who must eat, pay rent, hire colleagues, and keep the lights on. For
decades the industry has pretended that these two facts must be traded against one another:
either you publish under a permissive license and surrender the commercial value of your
work to whoever copies it fastest, or you close the source and surrender the trust of
everyone who must run it.

This License rejects that false choice.

This License makes the **source code public and permanently visible**, so that any person on
Earth may read it, learn from it, audit it, teach with it, cite it, criticize it, and propose
improvements to it — without asking anyone for anything. It simultaneously keeps the **right
to run the software as a deployed system** under the control of the Author, so that
deployment is a deliberate, recorded, individually-granted act rather than an accident of
copying.

The instrument by which that grant is made is the **Letter of Software Deployment Approval
(LOSDA)**. A LOSDA is not a purchase receipt, not a click-through, and not a courtesy. It is
a signed permission instrument with an identifier, a scope, a term, a register entry, and a
revocation path. This License and the LOSDA constitute a two-part framework: the License
governs what everyone may do; the LOSDA governs who may deploy, where, how, and for how long.

Together they form the **PASVL/LOSDA framework**: a public-availability, permission-gated,
professionally governed licensing system for the next era of software distribution.

**The Author retains all rights not expressly granted. There is no implied license. Reading
is free. Deployment is licensed.**

