### ARTICLE 1 — DEFINITIONS

Capitalized terms have the meanings set out in this Article. Terms defined in the singular
include the plural and vice versa. "Including" means "including without limitation".

**1.1 "Affiliate"** means, with respect to an entity, any other entity that controls, is
controlled by, or is under common control with that entity, where "control" means direct or
indirect ownership of more than fifty percent (50%) of the voting interests, or the power to
direct the management and policies of the entity.

**1.2 "Author"** means the natural person or legal entity that created the Work and holds the
economic rights in it, or, where the Work has been assigned or contributed to BSDC, BSDC
acting as rights holder. Where a Work has multiple Authors, each is an Author of the entirety
of the Work unless the NOTICE states otherwise.

**1.3 "BSD C" or "Steward"** means the Bangladesh Software Development Community, a
community organization registered and operating under the laws of the People's Republic of
Bangladesh, acting in its capacity as steward, publisher, registrar, and custodian of this
License and of the LOSDA framework, and not as a party to any commercial transaction between
an Author and a licensee.

**1.4 "Commercial Deployment"** means any Deployment that is intended to generate, or that
reasonably can be expected to generate, directly or indirectly, revenue, cost savings,
competitive advantage, or other commercial benefit for the deployer or for any third party,
including Deployment in the course of a trade, business, profession, or public procurement.

**1.5 "Contribution"** means any code, documentation, design, specification, test, artwork, or
other material that You intentionally submit to an Author or to BS C for inclusion in, or for
the improvement of, a Work, by any means including pull request, patch, issue attachment,
mailing list, chat message, or code review comment.

**1.6 "Contributor"** means a person or entity that makes a Contribution.

**1.7 "Deployment"** means any act of executing, loading into memory for execution, running,
installing for operational purposes, hosting, serving, exposing over a network, embedding,
flashing, distributing in executable form, or otherwise putting a Work or a Derivative Work
into operational use, in whole or in substantial part, whether for internal purposes, for
external service provision, or for inclusion in a product, device, or system. Deployment
includes Deployment by a service provider on behalf of another person. Deployment does not
include the acts permitted under Sections 3 (Visibility Grant) and 6 (Evaluation Use).

**1.8 "Deployment Scope"** means the totality of permissions set out in a LOSDA, including
the Licensed Work, the permitted Deployment type, the Territory, the Field of Use, the
scale limits, the Term, and any conditions or restrictions stated in that LOSDA.

**1.9 "Derivative Work"** means any work that is based on, incorporates, adapts, translates,
modifies, or otherwise is derived from a Work or any part of it, including any Modification,
any work that links to or combines with the Work, and any work in which the Work's expressive
content is recast, transformed, or adapted, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable
copyright law.

**1.10 "Distribution"** means the transfer of a copy of a Work or Derivative Work to another
person, in source or executable form, by any means, whether or not for consideration.

**1.11 "Evaluation Use"** means a temporary, private, non-commercial, non-production use of a
Work as set out in Section 6.

**1.12 "Effective Date"** means the date on which a LOSDA takes effect as stated in the LOSDA
Record, being not earlier than the date of its issuance.

**1.13 "Enforcement Register"** means the public, redacted record maintained by the Steward
under Article 20 listing Notices of Non-Compliance, revocations, and other enforcement
actions taken under this License.

**1.14 "Fork"** means a copy of a repository of a Work created within a public code hosting
platform, together with its associated history, created for the purpose of viewing,
experimenting, proposing Contributions, or preserving a record.

**1.15 "Hosted Service"** means any Deployment in which the functionality of a Work is made
available to persons other than the deployer, whether over a network, by API, by interface, by
batch job, or by any other means.

**1.16 "License"** means this Public Availability with Source-Code Visibility License,
Version 1.0, together with all Appendices, any NOTICE adopted by the Author, and any
authoritative amendment published by the Steward under Article 26.

**1.17 "LOSDA"** means a Letter of Software Deployment Approval issued under Article 10 and
Appendix A, in the form published by the Steward, and identified by a unique LOSDA ID.

**1.18 "LOSDA Record"** means the authoritative machine-readable record of a LOSDA held in
the LOSDA Registry, which prevails over any summary, copy, PDF, email, or screenshot in case
of conflict.

**1.19 "LOSDA Registry"** means the registry maintained by the Steward at
`registry/losda-registry.json` in the canonical repository, together with any successor
system publicly designated by the Steward.

**1.20 "Machine Learning Use"** means the use of a Work, in whole or in part, as training
data, fine-tuning data, evaluation data, embedding input, or as a source of synthetic data
generation, for the development or improvement of any machine learning model, regardless of
model architecture, regardless of whether the output is source code, and regardless of
whether the resulting model is distributed publicly, privately, or as a service.

**1.21 "Modification"** means any change to a Work, including addition, deletion, renaming,
refactoring, translation, porting, patching, configuration that alters behavior, and
combination with other software.

**1.22 "Non-Commercial Purpose"** means a purpose that is not primarily intended for or
directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation. Deployment by a for-profit
entity is presumed Commercial Deployment; Deployment by a non-profit, charitable,
educational, or governmental entity may be Non-Commercial only where the Deployment is not
part of an income-generating activity and is not performed on behalf of a for-profit entity.

**1.23 "NOTICE"** means a file named `NOTICE` or `PASVL-NOTICE.md` placed at or near the root
of a Work's repository, or, where no such file exists, the notice header in the Work's source
files, which states the Author's identity, contact channel, and the Mode under Section 6.2.

**1.24 "Notice of Non-Compliance" or "NNC"** means a formal written notice issued under
Section 20.4 identifying an alleged Violation and the cure period applicable to it.

**1.25 "Production Deployment"** means any Deployment that is not Evaluation Use and that is
used for real operational purposes, including any Deployment serving real users, processing
real data, supporting real business processes, or forming part of a product offered to
others.

**1.26 "Publicly Available"** means that the Source Code of a Work is accessible to the
general public without payment, registration, or confidentiality obligation, through a public
repository or an equivalent publicly accessible location.

**1.27 "Redistribution"** means Distribution to any person, including Distribution of a
Derivative Work and Distribution in executable, containerized, or bundled form.

**1.28 "Registry Custodian"** means the person or persons appointed by the Steward under
Article 20 and the Registry Policy to operate the LOSDA Registry.

**1.29 "Reliance Period"** means the period described in Section 19.2 during which a
compliant Deployment Licensee may continue existing Deployment after a revocation or
termination.

**1.30 "Revocation"** means the withdrawal of a LOSDA by the issuing Author, in whole or in
part, in accordance with Article 10 and Section 18.7.

**1.31 "Service Bureau Use"** means any arrangement in which the deployer permits a third
party to use a Work's functionality, directly or indirectly, as a substitute for the third
party obtaining its own LOSDA, whether by shared instance, white-labelling, agency
arrangement, resale, capacity resale, or automated provisioning on the third party's request.

**1.32 "Software" or "Work"** means the software, source code, documentation, data files,
configuration, assets, and other materials made available by the Author under this License,
including all Modifications and Derivative Works made by the Author.

**1.33 "Source Code"** means the preferred form of a Work for making modifications to it,
including all build scripts, schemas, configuration required for reproducible builds, and
interface definition files.

**1.34 "Standard LOSDA"** means a LOSDA issued on the Steward's standard terms for the
applicable LOSDA Class, without negotiated variations to the standard conditions.

**1.35 "Substantial Portion"** means any portion of a Work that is quantitatively or
qualitatively material to the Work's functionality, value, or distinctiveness, including any
module, library, component, algorithm, schema, model, or dataset that is not trivial,
independently trivial to recreate, or purely decorative.

**1.36 "Territory"** means the geographic, jurisdictional, or organizational area within which
a LOSDA permits Deployment.

**1.37 "Third-Party Components"** means software, libraries, data, or assets included in or
required by a Work that are governed by their own licenses, as identified in the Work's
package manifests or third-party notices.

**1.38 "Trademarks"** means the names, logos, trade dresses, service marks, and domain names
associated with a Work or with BSDC, including the "PASVL", "LOSDA", and "BSD C" designations.

**1.39 "Verification URL"** means the stable public URL at which the current validity and
scope of a LOSDA can be checked.

**1.40 "Violation"** means any act or omission that breaches this License or a LOSDA,
including any act that exceeds the Deployment Scope of a LOSDA.

**1.41 "You"** means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License, and
any Affiliate of that entity whose acts are directed or controlled by it. "Your" has a
corresponding meaning.

