### ARTICLE 2 — ACCEPTANCE, ELIGIBILITY, AND ORDER OF PRECEDENCE

**2.1 Acceptance by conduct.** You accept this License by any act that exercises a right
granted under it, including cloning, forking, downloading, reading, building, or executing a
Work. If You do not accept this License, You must not exercise any right granted under it.

**2.2 Acceptance by entity.** If You accept this License on behalf of an entity, You represent
that You have authority to bind that entity, and "You" includes that entity and its
Affiliates acting on its behalf.

**2.3 Eligibility.** This License is available to any natural person or legal entity, except
a person or entity that is (a) subject to sanctions that prohibit the transaction; (b)
excluded under Section 22; or (c) the subject of an active suspension under Section 18.9, in
respect of the suspended rights only.

**2.4 No registration required for the Visibility Grant.** No account, registration, payment,
or permission is required to exercise the rights granted under Article 3.

**2.5 Order of precedence.** In the event of conflict, the following order prevails:
(a) mandatory provisions of applicable law;
(b) the LOSDA Record, as to the terms of that LOSDA only;
(c) this License;
(d) the NOTICE;
(e) any README, documentation, or marketing material.

**2.6 Relationship to Third-Party Components.** Third-Party Components remain governed by
their own licenses. This License does not grant rights in Third-Party Components beyond those
their own licenses provide, and does not restrict rights that their own licenses
irrevocably grant.

**2.7 Relationship to platform terms.** Use of a public code hosting platform is also subject
to that platform's terms of service. This License does not purport to override platform
terms, and nothing in this License grants permission that the platform terms withhold. See
Article 28 and `legal/platform-reality.md`.

