### ARTICLE 3 — THE VISIBILITY GRANT

Subject to Your compliance with Article 4, the Author grants to You, free of charge,
worldwide, a perpetual, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable
license to do the following with a Work, for any purpose including commercial purposes:

**3.1 Read and study.** To read, view, display, and study the Source Code of the Work.

**3.2 Audit and verify.** To audit, inspect, analyze, test for vulnerabilities, verify
behavior, and evaluate the security, privacy, and correctness of the Work, subject to
Article 8.

**3.3 Clone, fork, and archive.** To clone, Fork, mirror, and archive the Work, and to retain
copies for reference and record-keeping. Archived copies remain subject to this License and
do not expand Your rights.

**3.4 Learn and teach.** To learn from the Work and to use it as teaching material, in
lectures, courses, textbooks, tutorials, workshops, and academic publications, provided that
such use does not involve Deployment and complies with Article 4.

**3.5 Cite and comment.** To quote portions of the Source Code for the purposes of citation,
criticism, review, commentary, journalism, research, or comparative analysis, with
attribution and in a manner that does not create a competing deployment.

**3.6 Propose changes.** To prepare and submit Contributions and to create Forks for that
purpose, subject to Article 12.

**3.7 Build for verification.** To compile, build, or execute the Work in a controlled,
private, non-production environment solely to verify that it does what it claims, within the
limits of Section 6.

**3.8 Report.** To report defects, vulnerabilities, licensing concerns, or misconduct to the
Author, the Steward, or a competent authority.

**3.9 Personal study copy.** To keep and use a private copy on Your own devices for personal
study, provided that the copy is not used for Deployment.

**3.10 No other rights.** No right to Deploy, to Distribute in executable form, to provide a
Hosted Service, to Redistribute, to sublicense, or to commercialize the Work is granted
under this Article. Those rights are reserved under Article 5.

