### ARTICLE 4 — CONDITIONS OF THE VISIBILITY GRANT

The Visibility Grant is conditioned on the following. Failure to comply suspends the
Visibility Grant automatically and constitutes a Violation.

**4.1 Attribution.** Where You distribute, publish, quote, or present the Work or any
Substantial Portion outside Your own organization, You must retain and display the Author's
copyright notice, this License's name and version, the LOSDA requirement statement, and a
link to the canonical repository.

**4.2 No removal of notices.** You must not remove, obscure, alter, or circumvent any
copyright notice, license header, attribution statement, NOTICE file, or digital watermark
included in or on the Work.

**4.3 No misrepresentation.** You must not state or imply that the Work is licensed under any
other license, that it is "open source" within the meaning of the Open Source Definition,
that it is free to deploy, or that You have authority to grant rights in it.

**4.4 No relicensing.** You must not relicense, sublicense, or purport to grant any rights in
the Work, in whole or in Substantial Portion, to any third party, except as expressly
permitted by this License or by a LOSDA.

**4.5 No laundering.** You must not incorporate a Substantial Portion of the Work into
another work in order to avoid the deployment restrictions of this License, whether by
renaming, refactoring, transpiling, extracting, minifying, bundling, or translating the Work
into another language or representation.

**4.6 No deployment.** You must not Deploy the Work except as permitted by Article 6 or by a
valid LOSDA.

**4.7 No automated extraction.** You must not use automated means to extract, scrape, or
harvest the Work's Source Code for Machine Learning Use, except as permitted by Article 14.

**4.8 Compliance with law.** You must comply with all applicable laws in exercising rights
under this License.

**4.9 Respect for persons.** You must not use the Work, its Source Code, its documentation, or
its community spaces to harass, defame, discriminate against, or endanger any person, or to
facilitate serious harm.

---

### ARTICLE 5 — RESERVED RIGHTS: DEPLOYMENT REQUIRES A LOSDA

**5.1 Reservation.** All rights not expressly granted are reserved by the Author. Without
limiting the foregoing, the right to Deploy is expressly reserved and is granted only by a
LOSDA issued under Article 10.

**5.2 No implied license.** No license may be implied from the Author's conduct, from
tolerance of past Deployment, from the availability of the Source Code, from the presence of
the Work in a public repository, from the existence of a Fork, from the absence of a
technical restriction, or from the Author's failure to enforce this License in any instance.

**5.3 Deployment without a LOSDA is a Violation.** Any Deployment without a valid LOSDA,
other than as permitted by Section 6, is a material breach of this License, an infringement
of the Author's rights where the Work is protected, and a breach of the deployment
conditions of this License.

**5.4 Consideration and formation.** A LOSDA forms a binding agreement between the Author and
the licensee, supported by the consideration stated in the LOSDA (which may be a fee, a
reciprocal obligation, or the licensee's undertakings under Article 11). A LOSDA that states
no consideration is nonetheless binding as a unilateral permission instrument granted in
reliance on the licensee's undertakings.

**5.5 Instrument, not sale.** A LOSDA grants permission; it does not transfer ownership of
the Work, does not assign copyright, and does not create a partnership, joint venture,
agency, franchise, or employment relationship.

