### ARTICLE 12 — CONTRIBUTIONS

**12.1 Inbound license.** By submitting a Contribution, You grant the Author and the Steward a
perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable, non-exclusive license to use, reproduce,
modify, adapt, publish, distribute, sublicense, and relicense the Contribution, in any form
and for any purpose, including for the commercial licensing of the Work under this License
and under any LOSDA.

**12.2 Copyright retention.** You retain copyright in Your Contribution. No assignment is
required unless You separately agree to one in writing.

**12.3 Representations.** You represent that (a) You are legally entitled to grant the license
in Section 12.1; (b) the Contribution is Your original work or is submitted with the necessary
permissions; (c) the Contribution does not infringe third-party rights; and (d) if Your
employer has rights in the Contribution, You have obtained permission or the employer has
waived those rights.

**12.4 Developer Certificate of Origin.** Contributions must be accompanied by a sign-off
certifying the Developer Certificate of Origin, version 1.1, unless the Author's CONTRIBUTING
file requires an alternative.

**12.5 Contributions under this License.** Contributions become part of the Work and are
licensed to the public under this License. Contributors do not acquire any deployment rights
by contributing; a Contributor who wishes to Deploy must obtain a LOSDA like anyone else.

**12.6 No obligation to accept.** The Author may accept, reject, or modify any Contribution
without giving reasons and without liability.

**12.7 Attribution of contributors.** The Author must maintain a contributors file and credit
Contributions where reasonably practicable, but the absence of credit is not a breach.

**12.8 Contribution misconduct.** Contributions that contain malicious code, undisclosed
tracking, license laundering, or plagiarized material are a Violation and may be reported
under Article 20.

