### ARTICLE 13 — PROHIBITED CONDUCT AND ANTI-CIRCUMVENTION

The following are prohibited and constitute Violations:

**13.1 Unlicensed Deployment.** Deploying a Work without a valid LOSDA, other than as
permitted by Article 6, 7, 8, or 9.

**13.2 Scope abuse.** Deploying outside the Deployment Scope, including exceeding scale limits,
serving users in a Territory not granted, or entering a Field of Use not granted.

**13.3 Licensing laundering.** Removing, replacing, or obscuring license notices in order to
present a Work or Derivative Work as licensed under different terms.

**13.4 Fork abuse.** Using a Fork, mirror, or archived copy to Deploy outside the terms of a
LOSDA, or maintaining a Fork for the purpose of circumventing revocation.

**13.5 Service Bureau Use.** Providing Service Bureau Use without a LOSDA that expressly
permits it.

**13.6 Sublicensing.** Granting any third party rights in a Work, or representing to a third
party that it may Deploy the Work, without authority.

**13.7 Circumvention of technical measures.** Defeating, disabling, or bypassing any license
enforcement mechanism, deployment gate, watermark, or telemetry consent mechanism included in
a Work, except as permitted by Article 8.

**13.8 Fraudulent records.** Presenting a forged, altered, expired, superseded, or revoked
LOSDA, or registering a LOSDA with false information.

**13.9 Misrepresentation.** Falsely claiming to be an Author, a Steward, a Registry Custodian,
or an authorized issuer of LOSDAs.

**13.10 Malicious modification.** Introducing malicious code, backdoors, unauthorized data
exfiltration, or destructive functionality into a Work or a Contribution.

**13.11 Model laundering.** Using a Work to train or distil a model in order to reproduce its
functionality while avoiding the deployment conditions of this License, except as permitted
by Article 14.

**13.12 Harassment of enforcers.** Retaliating against any person who reports a Violation,
participates in an enforcement proceeding, or refuses to participate in a Violation.

**13.13 Sanctions evasion.** Using the Work in violation of Article 22.

**13.14 Unconscionable use.** Using the Work for mass surveillance, autonomous weapons
targeting, or other uses prohibited by the Steward's Ethics Policy where the applicable LOSDA
incorporates that policy.

