### ARTICLE 14 — MACHINE LEARNING AND AUTOMATED PROCESSING

**14.1 Default rule.** Machine Learning Use of a Work requires a LOSDA of Class M, unless
permitted by Section 14.2.

**14.2 Permitted without a LOSDA.** You may use a Work for Machine Learning Use where:
(a) the use is limited to research permitted by Article 7 and the resulting model is not
deployed commercially; or
(b) the use is for security testing or vulnerability detection conducted under Article 8; or
(c) the Author has stated in the NOTICE that Machine Learning Use is permitted, in which case
the terms stated apply.

**14.3 Attribution of training data.** Where Machine Learning Use is permitted, You must
record the use of the Work in the model card, dataset card, or equivalent documentation, and
must not represent the resulting model as independent of the Work.

**14.4 No output laundering.** You must not use a model trained on a Work to generate a
substitute for the Work for the purpose of avoiding a LOSDA.

**14.5 Automated agents.** Automated agents, crawlers, and code-generation systems must
respect this Article and must not treat the public availability of the Source Code as
permission for Machine Learning Use.

**14.6 Reserved consideration.** The Author reserves the right to require a Class M LOSDA
with negotiated terms for large-scale or commercial Machine Learning Use, and to decline such
use.

