### ARTICLE 18 — TERM, TERMINATION, CURE, AND REINSTATEMENT

**18.1 Term of the License.** The Visibility Grant runs for the duration of the copyright in
the Work, unless terminated earlier under this Article.

**18.2 Termination for breach.** This License and all rights granted under it terminate
automatically, without notice, upon Your material breach of Article 4, Article 5, Article 11,
Article 12, Article 13, or Article 14, subject to the cure rights in Section 18.4.

**18.3 Termination of a LOSDA.** A LOSDA terminates on (a) expiry of its term; (b) Revocation
under Section 18.7; or (c) the licensee's material breach, subject to cure.

**18.4 Cure.** Where a breach is capable of cure, the breaching party may cure within thirty
(30) days of receiving an NNC, or such longer period as the NNC specifies, and the termination
is suspended during the cure period. Cure requires (a) cessation of the breach, (b)
remediation of its effects where reasonably possible, and (c) written confirmation to the
issuing authority. Breaches that are incapable of cure, including fraudulent LOSDA use,
malicious code introduction, and knowing circumvention, are not curable.

**18.5 Restitution on termination.** On termination, You must cease all Deployment, remove
executable copies from production systems, and, where the Author requires, certify cessation
in writing. You may retain archival copies for legal-record purposes only.

**18.6 Survival.** Sections 4.1, 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5, 12.1, 16.1 through 16.6, 18.5, 18.6,
Article 19, Article 20, Article 21, Article 22, Article 23, Article 24, and Article 25
survive termination.

**18.7 Revocation of a LOSDA.** The issuing authority may revoke a LOSDA, in whole or in part,
only on the following grounds:
(a) material breach of the LOSDA or of this License;
(b) fraudulent or materially false information in the LOSDA application or Registry record;
(c) use of the Work in a manner that causes, or is reasonably likely to cause, substantial
harm to persons, to the Author, to the Steward, or to the integrity of the framework;
(d) non-payment of fees after thirty (30) days' written notice, where fees apply;
(e) a requirement of law, court order, or sanctions; or
(f) the licensee's persistent conduct that brings the framework into disrepute, following a
final finding under Article 20.

**18.8 Procedure for revocation.** Revocation requires (a) written notice stating the grounds
and the evidence relied on; (b) a thirty (30) day opportunity to respond, except in urgent
cases under Section 18.10; (c) a reasoned decision by the issuing authority, reviewed by a
second reviewer appointed by the Steward; (d) recording in the Registry; and (e) notice of
the right of appeal under `governance/APPEALS.md`.

**18.9 Suspension.** Pending investigation, the issuing authority may suspend a LOSDA for up
to thirty (30) days, extendable once by thirty (30) days, where there is credible evidence of
a serious Violation. Suspension must be recorded in the Registry with the reason.

**18.10 Urgent action.** Where a Deployment presents an imminent risk of serious harm, the
issuing authority may act immediately and must provide the notice and hearing described in
Section 18.8 within five (5) business days after acting.

**18.11 Reinstatement.** A party whose rights were terminated or whose LOSDA was revoked may
be reinstated:
(a) automatically, if the breach is cured within the cure period and the party complies
prospectively;
(b) on application, where the Steward's Reinstatement Panel finds that reinstatement is
consistent with the purposes of this License; or
(c) on the Author's written election.
Reinstatement is prospective and does not excuse liability for past breaches.

**18.12 Good-faith first-breach reinstatement.** A first-time, good-faith, non-commercial
breach that is cured within thirty (30) days of notice results in automatic reinstatement,
provided the breaching party did not conceal the breach.

**18.13 Termination does not affect third parties.** The termination of Your rights does not
terminate the rights of other compliant beneficiaries, and does not affect rights validly
granted under other LOSDAs.

