### ARTICLE 25 — GENERAL PROVISIONS

**25.1 Severability.** If any provision is held invalid or unenforceable, it must be modified to the
minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable, and the remaining provisions continue in
full force.

**25.2 Entire agreement.** This License, together with the NOTICE and any applicable LOSDA,
constitutes the entire agreement regarding the Work and supersedes prior understandings
regarding licensing.

**25.3 No waiver.** Failure or delay in exercising a right is not a waiver. A waiver is
effective only if in writing and signed by the waiving party, and applies only to the specific
instance.

**25.4 Assignment.** You may not assign or transfer this License or a LOSDA without the
Author's prior written consent, which must be recorded in the Registry. The Author may assign
its rights to a successor in interest provided the successor assumes the Author's obligations
under this License and the Registry is updated.

**25.5 Notices.** Notices to the Author must be sent to the contact channel stated in the
NOTICE. Notices to a licensee are effective when sent to the contact address in the LOSDA
Record. Notices to the Steward must be sent to the address published in `GOVERNANCE.md`.

**25.6 Force majeure.** Neither party is liable for delay or failure caused by events beyond
its reasonable control, provided it notifies the other party and mitigates the effect.

**25.7 No agency.** Nothing in this License creates an agency, partnership, joint venture, or
fiduciary relationship, except the limited issuing agency under Section 10.2.

**25.8 Third-party beneficiaries.** Except as stated in Section 25.9, no person other than the
parties has rights under this License.

**25.9 Beneficiary standing.** Contributors to a Work and BSDC are intended third-party
beneficiaries of Article 4, Article 11, and Article 13 and may enforce those provisions,
subject to Article 20.

**25.10 Headings.** Headings are for convenience only and do not affect interpretation.

**25.11 Further assurances.** Each party must execute such further documents as are reasonably
necessary to give effect to this License or a LOSDA.

**25.12 Cumulative remedies.** Remedies are cumulative and not exclusive, subject to Article
21.

**25.13 Anti-bribery and integrity.** Neither party may offer, solicit, or accept any improper
advantage in connection with a LOSDA or an enforcement decision.

**25.14 Publicity.** A licensee may state factually that it holds a LOSDA, and may use the
official badges under Article 17, but may not describe the relationship as a partnership or
endorsement.

**25.15 Counterparts and electronic signature.** LOSDAs may be issued and signed
electronically, including by cryptographic signature, and in counterparts, each of which is an
original.

