### ARTICLE 26 — VERSIONING, AMENDMENT, AND COMPATIBILITY

**26.1 Version identity.** Each version of this License is identified by a version number.
This document is Version 1.0. The version applicable to a Work is the version stated in its
NOTICE or, where no version is stated, the version published at the time the version of the
Work was released.

**26.2 No unilateral amendment of granted rights.** The Steward may publish amendments only in
accordance with the Amendment Process in `governance/AMENDMENT-PROCESS.md`, which requires a
public RFC, a minimum forty-five (45) day comment period, and the approval of the License
Council by a two-thirds majority.

**26.3 Effect of amendments.** A published amendment applies prospectively to new versions of
a Work and does not retroactively reduce rights validly granted under a prior version, except
where required by law or by a court order.

**26.4 Corrections.** Typographical corrections, clarifications that do not change substance,
and updates to URLs or contact details may be made by the Steward on notice, without the full
amendment process, provided the change is logged in `CHANGELOG.md` and does not alter rights.

**26.5 Compatibility.** A Work may be combined with works under the licenses listed in
Appendix C to the extent stated there. Any other combination does not grant rights in
Third-Party Components and may create obligations You must satisfy independently.

**26.6 Relicensing by the Author.** The Author may release later versions of the Work under
different terms, provided that the release of a later version does not withdraw the rights
granted in respect of earlier releases under Section 19.5.

**26.7 Successor framework.** If the Steward ceases to operate, the License Council must
appoint a successor steward or transfer the Registry and framework to a suitable institution,
and must publish a notice of transition.

