### ARTICLE 27 — THE STEWARD AND THE LICENSE COUNCIL

**27.1 Role of the Steward.** The Steward (a) publishes and versions this License; (b)
maintains the LOSDA Registry and the Enforcement Register; (c) publishes templates, guidance,
and the LOSDA specification; (d) operates the appeals and reinstatement processes; (e)
publishes an annual transparency report; and (f) holds the trademarks of the framework.

**27.2 Limits on the Steward.** The Steward must not (a) issue a LOSDA for a Work without
authority under Section 10.2; (b) revoke a LOSDA except as an issuing authority or under
Article 18; (c) disclose confidential Registry information except as permitted by Article 23;
or (d) use the framework to obtain an unfair commercial advantage.

**27.3 License Council.** The License Council is the governing body established in
`GOVERNANCE.md`. It approves amendments, appoints the Registry Custodian, oversees
enforcement integrity, and hears final appeals where an appeal panel is not independent.

**27.4 Conflicts of interest.** Members of the License Council, Registry Custodians, and
appeal panellists must disclose conflicts and recuse themselves, in accordance with
`governance/CONFLICT-OF-INTEREST.md`.

**27.5 Fiduciary standard.** The Steward and the License Council must act in the interests of
the framework as a whole, balancing the interests of Authors, deployers, contributors, and the
public.

**27.6 Dissolution.** On dissolution of the Steward, the Registry, the Enforcement Register,
the trademarks, and the right to publish this License vest in a successor institution selected
by the License Council, and failing that, in a court-appointed trustee. No dissolution may
retroactively reduce rights granted under Article 3.

---

### ARTICLE 28 — INTERPRETATION AND LANGUAGE

**28.1 Purposive interpretation.** This License must be interpreted to give effect to its
purposes: public visibility, auditable transparency, and permission-gated deployment.

**28.2 No contra proferentem against the framework.** Ambiguity in a LOSDA is resolved against
expansion of the licensee's rights, consistent with Section 10.5. Ambiguity in this License is
resolved to preserve the Visibility Grant, consistent with Article 3.

**28.3 Independence of provisions.** The Articles are independent. The unenforceability of the
deployment restriction in a jurisdiction does not affect the enforceability of the Visibility
Grant in that jurisdiction.

**28.4 Language.** This License is executed in English. Translations published by the Steward,
including the Bengali translation, are for convenience only; the English text prevails in case
of conflict. A translation may be designated authoritative for a specific jurisdiction by
notice of the Steward.

**28.5 Not open source.** This License is not an open-source license within the meaning of the
Open Source Definition, has not been submitted for OSI approval, and must not be described as
open source. It is a source-available license with permission-gated deployment.

**28.6 Not legal advice.** This License and the accompanying documentation do not constitute
legal advice. Authors and deployers should obtain independent legal advice for their
jurisdiction.

**28.7 Precedence of mandatory law.** Nothing in this License restricts rights that applicable
law grants to the public and that cannot be contractually excluded, including rights under
fair use, fair dealing, exhaustion, interoperability exceptions, and statutory reverse
engineering rights.

