### APPENDIX B — NOTICE HEADER AND MACHINE-READABLE IDENTIFIERS

**B.1 Source file header.** Each source file should carry:

```
Copyright (c) <year> <Author>
Licensed under the Public Availability with Source-Code Visibility License, Version 1.0
(PASVL-1.0). Source is public. Deployment requires a Letter of Software Deployment
Approval (LOSDA). See https://github.com/bsdc-info-bd/PASVL_LOSDA
SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-PASVL-1.0
```

**B.2 NOTICE file.** A minimal NOTICE file:

```
Work: <name>
Author: <name / entity / contact>
License: PASVL-1.0
Mode: S | U
Steward: BSD C (Bangladesh Software Development Community)
Issuing agent: <author | steward | both>
Deployment approval: required (LOSDA). Request: <contact or URL>
```

**B.3 Package manifests.** Because PASVL is not an OSI-approved identifier, use
`LicenseRef-PASVL-1.0` where a manifest accepts `LicenseRef-*` (for example in SPDX
expressions). Where a manifest requires a recognized value, use the most restrictive
recognized value and add a comment referencing this License.

